            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test demonstrates air leakage on the following house components:

-Windows: We noticed some air leakage on some windows especially on the units located in the basement.

-Door: We noticed air leakage on the double door on the main floor, no weather strips or protection were visible and therefore the top of the door was open at the junction of both doors. The addition of weather stripping might reduce the leakage and increase the airtightness of the door.

-Receptacles: At the moment of the infiltration test, we noticed leakage from the receptacles. We recommend the installation of insulation custom made for electrical boxes.

-Mechanical equipment chimneys: We noticed air leakage from the furnace chimney. This situation is normal.

-We also noticed air leakage from the bathrooms fans

</airSeal>
                <windows>At the moment of the inspection the windows in place are wooden double panes with metal spacer. We recommend the replacement of all windows by ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED units suitable for the northern climate and ZONE 3.</windows>
                <doors>We notices air leakage from the deck door located in the living room on the main floor. The exterior light was visible around the door. The addition of weather strips might help to reduce the gap between the door and the frame. If replacement of the unit, we recommend the use of an ENERGY STAR CERTIFIED product.</doors>
                <HeatingSystem>At the moment of the inspection the house was heated by 2 wood stove. We also noticed an oil furnace, but it was out of function. We recommend the installation of an Air source heat pump. This type of system can supply heat and cooling, and it can use three times less energy. We recommend consulting a specialist for the appropriate equipment. </HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
